1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:05,447
Choosing the Right Register My sales pitch was full of slang I

2
00:00:05,461 --> 00:00:08,500
said a product would be a hit and invited customers to pop

3
00:00:08,513 --> 00:00:13,803
into the shop Such phrases suited conversation but a formal report needed

4
00:00:13,816 --> 00:00:19,961
greater precision Calling a product positively perfect could conceal a gross exaggeration

5
00:00:20,868 --> 00:00:25,171
A puff of promotional praise was not evidence Nor should I call

6
00:00:25,184 --> 00:00:30,776
a competitor shady because its methods were unfamiliar Frequent repetition could make

7
00:00:30,789 --> 00:00:35,829
a label seem credible without making it fair We also discussed literally

8
00:00:35,987 --> 00:00:40,750
a word often used loosely in conversation In formal work its meaning

9
00:00:40,763 --> 00:00:45,539
should be clear An expression described as vulgar may be inappropriate for

10
00:00:45,553 --> 00:00:50,224
the audience Good style means choosing language whose tone and meaning fit

11
00:00:50,237 --> 00:00:50,987
the purpose
